well, there is the middle ground.  Just because something "goes beyond
attitudinals" does not mean that it is "beyond UI*".

"ga'iru'e" is acceptable but "koru'e".... what does that mean?  Does it make
sense to "modify" a non-ui with a UI?

I think at that point you're doing the standard 'ol "mi nelci do .iu" thing
where the UI isn't modifying the preceding word, it's just coloring it.

